{
 "_note": "Photo mockup scenes. Coordinates are pixels in the scene image. pts = TL,TR,BR,BL of the printable surface. mode: opaque (covers the printed sample), multiply (blank surface; shading shows through), shade (art multiplied by the -shade.webp luminance, clipped to its alpha). fit: reshape = the object is erased (plate = same photo with the printed objects removed) and redrawn at the artwork's true proportions inside the photo object (same area as the photo object, limited by grow [maxU,maxV] relative to it; anchor in 0..1 of the object; optional stack/shadow/rotate); scale = the photo region (object + hardware) is rescaled about anchor so the surface matches the artwork's proportions (axis x keeps height; max/min limit the change); cover: true = fill and crop; stretch: true = always stretch (curved panels); default = stretch when within 6%, else contain. clip = alpha image that the art is clipped to (curved paper). hole: 'hanger' cuts the door-hanger die line. rect = upright print area for apparel (art is fitted top-centre). Garment scenes recolour the alpha mask of -shade.webp.",
